  "limitations": [
    "Verus proves four production length-state transitions for all u64 values. The trait/closure adapter, first-Error retention, JSON extraction and syscall correspondence are not composed into a whole-API proof.",
    "The TLA model has two traversals, lengths 0..2 and at most two callbacks per pass. Hash equality is overapproximated by equal byte counts. It does not prove cryptography or arbitrary provider termination.",
    "Provider code must return; callback validation does not preempt infinite custom code. Failure may leave an unpublished tail; rollback is not promised.",
    "The 100 GB run is one publication, not a publication p99. Pooled range percentiles describe sequential full 256 MiB requests from three concurrent readers, excluding shorter final ranges; samples are correlated and not a latency bound.",
    "Payload repeats a random 8 MiB pattern. Generation and chunk-metadata setup are outside write timing; envelope hashing, framing and fsync are included. No cache eviction or external-load isolation.",
    "Native binary measurements cover the storage API, not Python tensor construction, queue RPC or physical TB throughput. No controlled before/after overhead estimate is inferred from earlier runs.",
    "Format documentation removed obsolete admission-cap claims; no new quotas or parser-memory guarantees were introduced."
  ],
